%N A399485 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * AO(k) / (2*k-1), where AO(k) = A007509(k)/A352395(k) is the k-th alternating odd harmonic number (or skew-harmonic number of the second kind).
%D A399485 J. Irving and N. Mullineux (eds.), Mathematics in Physics and Engineering, New York and London, Academic Press, 1959, p. 648, Problem 16.
%H A399485 Adán Cabello, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.72.012113">How much larger quantum correlations are than classical ones</a>, Physical Review A - Atomic, Molecular, and Optical Physics, Vol. 72, No. 1 (2005), Article 012113; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0409192">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:quant-ph/0409192, 2004-2005. See abstract and p. 4, eq. (16).
%H A399485 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 669.
%H A399485 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 10, eq. (28).
%H A399485 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399485 Equals 3*Pi^2/32 = 3*A244854 (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019).
%F A399485 Equals Integral_{x>=0} x^2 * BesselK(1,x)^2 dx (Irving and Mullineux, 1959).
%F A399485 Formulas from Shamos (2011):
%F A399485 Equals Sum_{k>=1} k^2*zeta(2*k)/4^k.
%F A399485 Equals Sum_{k>=1} (4*k^2)*(4*k^2+1)/(4*k^2-1)^3.
%F A399485 Equals Integral_{x>=1} arctan(x)/(1+x^2) dx.
%e A399485 0.925275412602127370515733531238389168935659319428824...
